<h2 id="hybrid-routing">Hybrid Auto-Routing</h2>
<p>
  With <code>RUNNER_BACKEND=auto</code> and <code>AUTO_ROUTE_VM=true</code>, you
  don't need to choose a single engine. The autoscaler inspects workflow labels
  and job names:
</p>
<pre
  class="code-block"><code># Standard unit test runs in ultra-fast Docker container (~0.3s)
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: [ self-hosted, local ]
    steps:
      - run: npm test

# Lighthouse / Browser E2E automatically routes to dedicated Linux VM!
jobs:
  audit:
    runs-on: [ self-hosted, local, browser ]  # Triggers: 'browser', 'e2e', 'lighthouse', 'systemd', 'vm'
    steps:
      - run: npx lhci autorun</code></pre>
